Create Group 09 — Typography & Content for the DevKit.

This group belongs to:

Layer 01 — Foundations & Interface Primitives.

Existing groups:

Group 01 — Interaction Controls
Group 02 — Form Controls
Group 03 — Selection Controls
Group 04 — Navigation Controls
Group 05 — Feedback & Status
Group 06 — Overlays & Surfaces
Group 07 — Data Display
Group 08 — Media & Visual Content

Use the DevKit Core Design Constitution as the immutable global foundation.

Do not redefine:
- font families
- font weights
- font sizes
- line heights
- letter spacing
- colors
- semantic colors
- spacing
- breakpoints
- radius
- elevation
- motion

All typography must consume the global typography tokens.

Create exactly these 10 components:

081 Text
082 Heading
083 Paragraph
084 Label
085 Caption
086 Link
087 Code
088 Code Block
089 Blockquote
090 Number Display

These are semantic and visual content primitives.

They must be usable inside:
- cards
- lists
- forms
- dialogs
- navigation
- tables
- dashboards
- settings
- detail views
- marketing surfaces
- documentation
- AI interfaces

Do not create:
- complete article pages
- complete documentation pages
- rich text editors
- markdown editors
- complete code editors
- complete typography settings pages

Those are higher-level components.

Typography must prioritize:
readability
hierarchy
scannability
consistency
accessibility
localization

Do not use typography as decoration.

Do not create arbitrary font sizes per component.

Do not use excessive font weights.

Do not make everything bold.

Use hierarchy through:
size
weight
spacing
position
semantic structure

Color should be secondary to typographic hierarchy.

Do not rely on color alone to communicate meaning.

All text components must support:
- Light
- Dark
- High Contrast
- RTL
- localization
- dynamic text scaling
- browser zoom
- accessibility technologies

Text must remain usable at:
200% zoom
large system font settings
long translations
narrow mobile widths

Do not assume English word lengths.

Avoid fixed-width text containers unless explicitly required.

Text wrapping must be intentional.

Do not create accidental horizontal scrolling.

Where truncation is used:
it must be deliberate
the full content must remain discoverable
accessibility must preserve the full value

Support:
single-line
multi-line
long-form
short-form

where relevant.

Typography must maintain readable line lengths.

Do not create extremely wide paragraphs on desktop.

Content containers should use the global reading-width tokens.

Do not force all text into centered layouts.

Default long-form reading content should generally use a comfortable reading measure.

Support:
LTR
RTL

Bidirectional text must render correctly.

Mixed content such as:
Arabic + English
numbers + text
URLs + text
code + prose

must remain understandable.

Links must be distinguishable from surrounding text.

Do not rely exclusively on color.

Interactive text must have:
hover
focus
visited where applicable
pressed where applicable

Focus must be clearly visible.

Code must use a suitable monospace token from the global typography system.

Do not introduce a random monospace font.

Code content must preserve whitespace where required.

Number Display must support:
large values
decimals
currency
percentages
negative values
localized number formats

Do not hardcode formatting to one locale.

Support:
loading
unknown
not available
zero
negative
very large values

without creating visual instability.

All text must remain accessible to screen readers.

Decorative text should not create unnecessary accessibility output.
